    "body": "The new Volvo EX60 has an EPA-estimated range of 312 miles, but in real-world conditions, it drove over 350 miles without stopping.\nVolvo EX60 beats EPA range in the real world\nVolvo calls the EX60 a “game changer” as its fastest-charging, longest-range electric vehicle to date.\nIn July, Volvo announced the 2027 EX60 P10 AWD received an official EPA certification with an estimated driving range of up to 330 miles, beating its own estimate of 322 miles.\nWhen fitted with the 22″ tires, the EX60 P10 AWD Ultra boasts an EPA-estimated range of 312 miles on a single charge.\nAdvertisement - scroll for more content\nDuring Edmunds recent EV Range Test , the AWD electric SUV proved it can drive further than advertised.\nThe EX60 P10 AWD (with 22″ tires) covered 352 miles on a single charge during the test, beating its EPA-estimated 312 miles by 13%.\nVolvo’s electric SUV also outperformed many luxury competitors that underwent the same test, including the Cadillac Lyriq AWD (319 miles) and Mercedes-Benz EQS+ 320 SUV (349 miles). However, it wasn’t enough to beat Mercedes’ new GLC 400 EV, which managed 392 miles.\n2027 Volvo EX60 (Source: Volvo)\nIt was also more efficient than expected, using just 28.8 kWh per 100 miles, beating its EPA-estimated 30 kWh per 100 miles.\nThe Edmunds EV Range Test is designed to offer a more accurate estimate of a vehicle’s range during real-world, everyday driving conditions. It consists of 60% city and 40% highway driving with an average speed of 40 mph.\nVolvo EX60 interior (Source: Volvo)\nThe vehicle stays within 5 mph of the posted speed limit, and the climate control is set on auto at 72 degrees.\nMeasuring 189.1″ long, 81.4″ wide, and 64.4″ high, with a 116.9″ wheelbase, the EX60 is about the size of a Tesla Model Y.\n2027 Volvo EX60 model | Starting Price * | Driving Range | Charging Time (10% to 80%) | 10 minutes of Charging | Max Charge Rate\nEX60 P6 Plus | $58,400 | 307 miles | 16 minutes | up to 155 miles | 320 kW\nEX60 P6 Ultra | $65,000 | 307 miles | 16 minutes | up to 155 miles | 320 kW\nEX60 P10 AWD Plus | $60,750 | 330 miles | 16 minutes | up to 165 miles | 370 kW\nEX60 P10 AWD Ultra | $67,350 | 330 miles | 16 minutes | up to 165 miles | 370 kW\nEX60 P12 AWD | N/A | 400 miles | 19 minutes | up to 173 miles | 370 kW\n2027 Volvo EX60 prices, driving range, and charging by variant (*Excluding $1,395 destination fee)\nThe base 2027 Volvo EX60 P6 starts at $58,400. The twin-motor EX60 P10 Plus Ultra starts at $60,750.\nBased on Volvo’s SPA3 platform with 800V fast charging, the P10 AWD version can add up to 165 miles in 10 minutes. The P6 can add up to 155 miles in 16 minutes.\nWant to see what’s available near you? You can click here to find available 2027 Volvo EX60 models in your area (trusted partner link).\nFTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links. More.\nStay up to date with the latest content by subscribing to Electrek on Google News . You’re reading Electrek— experts who break news about Tesla , electric vehicles, and green energy , day after day. Be sure to check out our homepage for all the latest news, and follow Electrek on Twitter , Facebook , and LinkedIn to stay in the loop. Don’t know where to start? Check out our YouTube channel for the latest reviews.",
